```"

The bug is in the null-handling of the axis-index lookup methods in `org.jfree.chart.plot.CategoryPlot`.

Evidence:
- `getDomainAxisIndex(CategoryAxis)` is documented with `axis` as “null not permitted”.
- Its implementation is only:
  ```java
  public int getDomainAxisIndex(CategoryAxis axis) {
      return this.domainAxes.indexOf(axis);
  }
  ```
- Dynamic verification confirmed that when `null` is passed, the method returns normally instead of throwing `IllegalArgumentException`, which directly explains `testGetDomainAxisIndex()` failing.

The paired failure strongly indicates the same defect pattern in:
- `getRangeAxisIndex(ValueAxis)`

Static evidence there is very strong:
- JavaDoc also says `axis` is “null not permitted”.
- Implementation has no null check:
  ```java
  public int getRangeAxisIndex(ValueAxis axis) {
      int result = this.rangeAxes.indexOf(axis);
      if (result < 0) {
          Plot parent = getParent();
          if (parent instanceof CategoryPlot) {
              CategoryPlot p = (CategoryPlot) parent;
              result = p.getRangeAxisIndex(axis);
          }
      }
      return result;
  }
  ```
- So `null` is looked up via `indexOf(null)` and may return normally instead of throwing, matching the failing `testGetRangeAxisIndex()` expectation.

Root cause:
- Both methods violate their documented contract by not rejecting `null` arguments with `IllegalArgumentException`.

Fix:
- Add an explicit null check at the start of both methods, e.g.
  ```java
  if (axis == null) {
      throw new IllegalArgumentException("Null 'axis' argument.");
  }
  ```

Best fix locations:
org.jfree.chart.plot.CategoryPlot.getDomainAxisIndex(org.jfree.chart.axis.CategoryAxis)
org.jfree.chart.plot.CategoryPlot.getRangeAxisIndex(org.jfree.chart.axis.ValueAxis)

